# Numsec Rules

When the user types `/numsec "..."` in chat, treat it as a structured command
defined in `NUMSEC.md`.

## Required context

- Read `NUMSEC.md` first.
- Then read `numsec/project.md`, `numsec/architecture.md` and the relevant
  `numsec/threats/THREAT-*/threat.md`.

## Running the analysis

- `numsec analyze . --ai-format` refreshes `numsec/threats/` and prints JSON.
- `numsec lint . --json` reports findings without writing files.
- Files starting with `<!-- generated by numsec` are regenerated: never edit them.

## Change policy

- For non-trivial security changes, create a proposal under
  `numsec/changes/<change-id>/` before implementing anything.

## Output expectations

- Respond with: what you read, what you plan to do, what files you changed.
